// src/v4/std/collection.dag
//
// Scope: container carriers grounded in algebras from std/algebra.dag —
//        the container-side operations are reads of those algebras,
//        never an enumerated per-op table (the NO-ENGINE STOP per
//        std/algebra.dag header U1). The two carriers have DIFFERENT
//        cardinality stories — read them honestly:
//          - List<T> = FreeMonoid<T>: a structurally finite sequence;
//            its cardinality (length) IS intrinsic to the carrier,
//            read by walking the Empty|Cons spine to bottom.
//          - Set<T> = characteristic function fn(T) -> Bool: a
//            subset-of-T carrier inhabiting BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>>. It
//            does NOT structurally encode finiteness — the universe
//            and complement constructions in the BooleanAlgebra grounding
//            are deliberately representable (BooleanAlgebra requires
//            them), so a `Set<Int>` such as "all positive ints" is a
//            valid value. Finite-cardinality is a REFINEMENT layer —
//            tracked as deferred (Wave-A2 scaffold item (2) below) and
//            out of scope for the carrier in this file.
//        This honest split was surfaced by the codex BLOCKING review
//        (#3169) flagging an earlier "finite subsets / count `true`
//        elements" over-claim on Set; the carrier is unchanged in
//        denotation (still T → Bool), the framing here is tightened to
//        match it (P1/P4/Practice-2).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_monoid (List) +
//         https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebra_of_sets (Set)
//
// Owns:
//   - List<T> — finite sequences (the free-monoid carrier over T;
//     finiteness is STRUCTURAL — every value bottoms out at Empty)
//   - Set<T>  — subset-of-T carrier, the characteristic function
//     fn(T) -> Bool (alias); inhabits BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>> via the
//     machine-readable `set_boolean_algebra` declaration below
//     (operator-ratified Wave-A2 Set grounding; Wave-A1 used an
//     equivalent Conj { member: fn(T)->Bool } spelling — dissolved
//     here to the callable carrier so pointwise lift lowers without
//     Prereq-X1.b call-on-field-of-parameter substrate debt).
//   - Map<K, V> — partial function K → 1+V with fail-closed lookup
//     (operator-ratified Wave-A2 Map split, Option A — #3169).
//   - set_boolean_algebra<T>() — the single BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>>
//     witness (generic fn, one authority per op — INVARIANTS P2).
//
// Deferred (tracked scaffold (🟡) — operator scope excludes these):
//   - FiniteSet<T> (or Set<T, n: Multiplicity>) — finite-cardinality
//     refinement; needs cardinality / enumerability substrate
//     (std/cardinality.dag Multiplicity + enumerability witness).
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Cardinality, Instantiation — the type-substrate
//     connectives the kernel uses to represent parameterized container
//     types in the type DAG. (No Cardinality TYPE is consumed; the
//     refinement-type carrier `Multiplicity` lives in std/cardinality.dag
//     — UNMERGED at #3163 — and is NOT consumed by collection.dag
//     today per the operator-ratified b2 decision.)
//   - std/algebra.dag: FreeMonoid<T>, BooleanAlgebra, BoundedLattice,
//     Lattice (List aliases FreeMonoid; Set's BooleanAlgebra witness
//     nests those structures per algebra.dag's refinement nesting).
//   - std/logic.dag: bool_boolean_algebra (pointwise lift source for
//     Set<T>'s meet/join/complement — epistemic stacking, not a second
//     truth-table authority).
//   - std/witness.dag: Witness<V> (Map.lookup codomain — fail-closed
//     partial function discipline per operator Option A, #3169).
//   (Bool and the type parameters T, K, V are kernel-ambient; Symbol
//   is substrate-ambient per std/node.dag K-1 — none is imported.)
//
// Header reconciliation — OPERATOR-RATIFIED b2 + Wave-A2, 2026-05-16:
//   Plain carriers List<T>, Set<T> (b2). Map<K,V> lands Wave-A2 after
//   witness.dag (Option A split, #3169). Set's carrier is spelled as
//   the function alias fn(T)->Bool so `set_boolean_algebra<T>()` can
//   lower the pointwise BooleanAlgebra witness without parametric
//   `data` (no v2 precedent) and without Prereq-X1.b (call-on-field of
//   a Set parameter). Wave-A1's Conj { member } record was modeling-
//   equivalent; dissolution here is carrier-shaping only, not a second
//   algebra authority.
//
// NO ENGINE — NO ENUMERATED OPS. There is deliberately no
// `list_concat` / `set_union` table here: those would be a parallel
// representation of structure std/algebra.dag already owns (the
// `kernel_algebra_profile` debt v3 carried, which std/algebra.dag's
// U1 note explicitly forbids — "not a name-keyed table lookup").
// Consumers read the algebra structures from algebra.dag and the
// carrier shapes here; ops are reads of that one authority, not
// table rows.
//
// Status: T-3 Wave-A1 modeled 2026-05-16 (#3169); Wave-A2 follow-up
//   2026-05-16 (snappy-stag-679): Map<K,V> + machine-readable Set
//   BooleanAlgebra witness. Splitting this file requires explicit
//   operator ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.collection


import v4.std.algebra { BooleanAlgebra, BoundedLattice, FreeMonoid, Lattice }
import v4.std.logic { bool_boolean_algebra }
import v4.std.witness { Witness }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// CARRIERS, NOT STRUCTURES. This file owns CONTAINER CARRIERS. The
// algebra structures they ground in (Monoid, BooleanAlgebra) are owned
// by std/algebra.dag; the inhabitant owns its OWN grounding here per
// std/algebra.dag's SCOPE note. List<T> grounds by TYPE ALIAS onto
// FreeMonoid<T> (the alias IS the Monoid inhabitance). Set<T> grounds
// as fn(T)->Bool with a MACHINE-READABLE witness `set_boolean_algebra`:
// a generic function declaration whose return type is
// BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>> — traversable by passes/lenses as the single
// authority for pointwise meet/join/complement/top/bottom (P2).
//
// NO NEW COPRODUCTS in this file for Wave-A2: Map<K,V> is a Conj
// record (Practice-4 ledger: N/A — not a Disj). List/Set introduce no
// new sum-type variants here.
//
// OPS FALL OUT OF GROUNDING — illustrated, not enumerated. The
// header names which algebra each carrier grounds in and how the
// ops project. Authoring those projections as concrete functions
// here would be the per-op table the brief forbids; they are
// pipeline-stage / lens reads of (carrier shape) ⊗ (algebra
// structure), consumed at the use site — except the single
// `set_boolean_algebra` witness, which IS the declared inhabitance
// edge (same role as `bool_boolean_algebra` in std/logic.dag).
//
// PARTIAL-ACCESS OPS — STOP on Outcome<T>. Any List / Set operation
// that would need the value-or-Diagnostic carrier (Outcome<T>) —
// e.g. an `unsafe_head` returning either a value or a
// "list-was-empty" Diagnostic — is a STOP per the operator-ratified
// pending-carrier substrate (not yet in v4). The CARRIERS themselves
// (List<T>, Set<T>) are Wave-A1-clean; Map<K,V> uses Witness<V> at
// the intentional partial channel (lookup) per Option A.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// List<T> — finite sequences of T. Structurally identical to
// FreeMonoid<T> (Empty | Cons { head, tail }); the alias IS the
// inhabitance — by being a FreeMonoid<T>, List<T> is a free-monoid
// carrier and inherits the Monoid structure with no parallel data
// instance (std/algebra.dag header: "Concrete sequence types ground
// by aliasing onto it (e.g. a text type onto FreeMonoid over a char
// type)").
//
// Operations (concat, length, fold, map, filter, head, tail) are
// STRUCTURAL READS of the FreeMonoid Empty/Cons constructors composed
// with a Monoid<T> the CALL SITE supplies (the brief's "Monoid for
// fold") — never enumerated here. The element type's algebra is the
// only authority for the per-call reduction; the carrier shape is
// the only authority for the recursion.
//
// Cardinality (length) is INTRINSIC to the carrier — read by walking
// the FreeMonoid spine, not declared as a refinement parameter on
// this type (per the operator-ratified b2 header note).
//
// This declaration is a type ALIAS onto a coproduct owned by
// std/algebra.dag (the FreeMonoid<T> = Empty | Cons ledger lives
// there). No new Practice-4 ledger applies — there is no new
// coproduct to dissolve at this layer.
type List<T> = FreeMonoid<T>


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Set<T> — a subset of T, modeled as a characteristic function T → Bool.
// Write `s(x)` for membership: x ∈ s iff `s(x) == true`. This is the
// textbook denotational form (Wikipedia "Algebra of sets"): a subset
// is a predicate on T.
//
// Spelled as the function carrier directly (not a Conj wrapper) so the
// pointwise BooleanAlgebra witness in `set_boolean_algebra<T>()` lowers
// under the existing v2 surface: parameters of type Set<T> are Arrow-
// typed, so they appear in callable_scope and `a(x)` invokes the
// characteristic function without Prereq-X1.b field-call substrate.
// Modeling equivalence: Wave-A1's `type Set<T> { member: fn(T)->Bool }`
// is the same carrier with a named field; the alias is the dissolution
// of that syntactic sugar for inhabitance lowering, not a semantic
// change.
//
// This carrier denotes ARBITRARY subsets, not "finite subsets" —
// `universe` and `complement` below are deliberately representable
// (BooleanAlgebra closure requires them), so a value like "all
// positive ints" is a valid `Set<Int>`. Finite-cardinality is a
// REFINEMENT layer deferred to scaffold item (2) (codex BLOCKING
// review on #3169 surfaced this distinction).
//
// Cardinality is NOT intrinsic to Set<T>: counting `true` elements
// requires an enumeration of T, and this carrier does not witness
// `T`'s enumerability. A finite-cardinality refinement (`FiniteSet<T>`
// or `Set<T, n: Multiplicity>`) is deferred alongside the cardinality /
// enumerability substrate (scaffold item (2) in the header).
//
// Coproduct dissolution — N/A: `Set<T>` is a type alias to Arrow, not
// a Disj.
type Set<T> = fn(T) -> Bool


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// set_boolean_algebra<T>() — MACHINE-READABLE BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>>
// witness (operator-ratified Wave-A2 task (b), 2026-05-16).
//
// Pointwise extension of `bool_boolean_algebra` (std/logic.dag) to
// Set<T> = fn(T)->Bool:
//   meet(a,b)   ≡ λx. bool_boolean_algebra....meet(a(x), b(x))
//   join(a,b)   ≡ λx. bool_boolean_algebra....join(a(x), b(x))
//   complement  ≡ λa. λx. bool_boolean_algebra.complement(a(x))
//   bottom      ≡ λx. false
//   top         ≡ λx. true
//
// The Boolean-algebra axioms are the grounded definition of
// BooleanAlgebra (algebra.dag); they are not re-stored here. Walking
// the returned record's fields yields the set operations — one
// authority each (INVARIANTS P2), same discipline as
// `bool_boolean_algebra` for Bool.
//
// Coproduct dissolution — N/A (returns a Conj-shaped algebra record,
// not a sum type).
fn set_boolean_algebra<T>() -> BooleanAlgebra<Set<T>> {
  BooleanAlgebra {
    bounded_lattice: BoundedLattice {
      lattice: Lattice {
        meet: fn(a, b) {
          fn(x) {
            bool_boolean_algebra.bounded_lattice.lattice.meet(a(x), b(x))
          }
        },
        join: fn(a, b) {
          fn(x) {
            bool_boolean_algebra.bounded_lattice.lattice.join(a(x), b(x))
          }
        }
      },
      top: fn(x) {
        True
      },
      bottom: fn(x) {
        False
      }
    },
    complement: fn(a) {
      fn(x) {
        bool_boolean_algebra.complement(a(x))
      }
    }
  }
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Map<K, V> — partial function K → 1+V (operator-ratified Wave-A2 Map
// split, Option A / #3169). Duplicate keys are structurally
// unrepresentable: `lookup` is a total function on K into Witness<V>;
// absence of a value is `Violates{...}`, not a second key binding.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — N/A: Map<K,V> is a Conj record (one field), not
// a sum type — no variant ledger applies.
type Map<K, V> {
  lookup: fn(K) -> Witness<V>
}
